{"author":{"id":"836d943203cf5a4f01ab5d4b4780de84949c43734f2256a167cc5931ae5d8c66"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794176301,"nonce":"cYGt5KTOnJhf27aeT93v87HbdjU=","message":"Landed on `roadmap-e90c710-integration` (a925e8d..b84edc1).\n\n**Changes**\n- src/gitbug/write.rs: new. close/reopen/set_state/comment/apply and WriteOp/StateTarget. Pure label-diff planners mirroring gb. Tests: planner unit tests, plus real git-bug temp-repo tests that skip with a printed reason when git-bug is absent.\n- src/gitbug/mod.rs: exports the write API, adds Closed and EmptyComment errors, and fixes parsing of `\"labels\": null`.\n- src/writes.rs: new WriteQueue/Ticket. Writes to one repo run in issue order; repos run in parallel; dropped tickets never stall the line. Unit tested.\n- src/lib.rs: registers the writes module.\n- src/app.rs: pending set, write_errors, comment drafts, Write/WriteDone/EditComment/SubmitComment messages. On success the issue is patched in the repo entry, the rows, the open pane, the detail cache and the snapshot; on failure the old state is kept. Spinner subscription while writes are pending. 5 new tests.\n- src/ui/detail.rs: pane buttons (In progress, Blocked, Clear state, Close, Reopen), Saving… indicator, inline error, markdown comment editor with a Comment button.\n- src/ui/screen.rs: row close/reopen icon toggle, pending spinner, inline row error.\n- src/ui/components.rs: choice_button and primary_button_maybe, so buttons can be disabled.\n- src/theme/style.rs: dimmed style for disabled primary and secondary buttons.\n\n**Gates:** tests ok · clippy ok · fmt ok\n**Review:** 1 findings — 0 auto, 1 by hand, 0 deferred\n\n**Decisions**\n- Write fns live in src/gitbug/write.rs, not cli.rs as the task said, since cli.rs is only the process runner.\n- Each write first calls show(), which also verifies the id prefix. Git-bug falls back to its last selected bug on an unmatched prefix, so the write then uses the resolved full id.\n- Real-repo tests found an existing bug: git-bug prints `\"labels\": null` for issues with no labels, which broke parsing. Fixed with null_as_empty and a test.\n- Per-repo ordering uses tickets taken synchronously in `update`. A plain tokio Mutex would not guarantee issue order, because spawned futures can poll in any order.\n- After a write the snapshot is saved with the old fingerprint, so the next 5s check reloads from git-bug. A write that fails partway (labels removed, then close fails) is corrected by that same check, with no rollback, as in gb.\n- Review finding: an error from a row-toggle write was only visible in the detail pane. It now also shows on the row, and the app.rs doc comment was corrected.\n- Comment drafts are kept per issue in App.drafts, so Esc or switching panes does not lose typing. Editing is read-only while a write is pending.","files":null}]}